        "original_id": "fc8ead98-7ff3-548d-901a-2fdae87bedf0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New York City, Lower Manhattan\n- Buildings: Central Park Place, World Trade Center, 888 7th Avenue\n- Companies: Pershing Square Capital Management\n- People: Bill Ackman, Emery Roth & Sons\n\nFacts:\n- The original World Trade Center was a complex of seven buildings in Lower Manhattan, New York City, United States, from 1973 to 2001.\n- Central Park Place is a 56-story condominium building in New York City.\n- 888 7th Avenue was designed by Emery Roth & Sons.\n- 888 7th Avenue is tied with Central Park Place as the 65th tallest building in New York City.\n- Pershing Square Capital Management is an American hedge fund management company founded and run by Bill Ackman.\n- Pershing Square Capital Management is located at 888 7th Avenue in New York.",
